          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "There are two ways to get one of each: HT and TH, so the probability is $\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
      "worked": "The four equally likely outcomes are HH, HT, TH and TT. The three categories in the statement are not equally likely: one of each includes both HT and TH.\n\n$$P(\\text{one of each})=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
